## 2. Most important new tests

These are the tests I consider most valuable for demonstrating that your changes to `Deduper.cs` work as intended.

### A. Duplicate email families with different attachment sets

This verifies that the tool preserves the most complete family and suppresses the less complete duplicate family entirely.

```
[Fact]
public void DuplicateEmailFamilyWithSubsetOfAttachments_IsSuppressedAsAWhole()
{
    var result = Deduper.Run(B(
        Email("E2", "c2", "email-bytes-2"),
        Attach("A2x", "c2", "E2", "x"),
        Email("E1", "c1", "email-bytes-1"),
        Attach("A1x", "c1", "E1", "x"),
        Attach("A1y", "c1", "E1", "y")));

    Assert.Equal(new[] { "A1x", "A1y", "E1" }, Ids(result));
    Assert.Equal(2, result.Suppressed);
    Assert.DoesNotContain(
        result.Rows, r => r.DocId == "E2" || r.DocId == "A2x");
}
```

Why it matters: A reviewer must not receive an email without the attachments associated with the version of that email retained by the deduplication process.

