### C. Nested attachments

```
[Fact]
public void NestedAttachments_ResolveToTopLevelEmailFamily()
{
    var result = Deduper.Run(B(
        Attach("A2", "c1", "A1", "nested"),
        Email("E1", "c1", "email-hash"),
        Attach("A1", "c1", "E1", "outer")));

    Assert.Equal(new[] { "A1", "A2", "E1" }, Ids(result));
    Assert.All(result.Rows, row =>
        Assert.Equal("E1", row.FamilyId));
    Assert.Equal(
        "A1", result.Rows.Single(r => r.DocId == "A2").ParentId);
}
```

Why it matters: The specification explicitly permits attachment hierarchies. This test verifies that a nested attachment receives the top-level email's `FamilyID`, even when the input documents are not ordered parent-first.

